  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target audience for this meme is individuals who are frustrated with financial institutions (banks) and who hold negative views toward Native American peoples, often rooted in historical grievances or contemporary political discourse. The meme appeals to those who identify with or sympathize with anti-bank sentiment and anti-Native American stereotypes, leveraging the historical figure of General Custer to symbolize aggressive, destructive force. The intended audience likely includes people who are politically or economically discontent, particularly those who perceive banks as exploitative and Native Americans as a symbol of historical resistance or conflict. The use of the word 'fuck' and the direct targeting of two distinct groups indicates the meme is designed for an audience that understands and accepts this hateful framing, often found in online communities that engage in political or economic protest rhetoric.",
